WEBVTT

00:08:58.375 --> 00:09:01.887
and was a champion disabled waterskier.

00:09:01.887 --> 00:09:05.134
But in 1989, he teamed up with Bill Joyce

00:09:05.134 --> 00:09:09.269
to develop a program that would read out

00:09:09.269 --> 00:09:11.020
what was on the computer screen

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:13.024
from the Net or from what was on the computer.

00:09:13.024 --> 00:09:16.531
It's called JAWS, Job Access With Speech,

00:09:16.531 --> 00:09:18.535
and it sounds like this.

00:09:18.535 --> 00:09:22.420
(JAWS speaking)

00:09:29.985 --> 00:09:31.748
Ron McCallum: Isn't that slow?